{
  "total": 73,
  "totalPage": 2,
  "page": 2,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b473",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 594,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"The Prophet ordered the construction of Masajid in all Dur and that they be kept clean and scented",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-594-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-594-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-594-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b474",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 595,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "(Another chain) from Hisham bin Urwah, from his father:\"That the Prophet ordered.\" And he mentioned similarly",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-595-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b475",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 596,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "(Another chain) from Hisham from Urwah, from his father:\"That the Prophet ordered.\" And he mentioned similarly",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-596-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b476",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 597,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \"The Salat during the night and the day is two and two",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-597-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-597-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-597-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-597-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b477",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 598,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "Asim bin Damrah said:\"We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah during the day. He said: 'You will not be able to do that.' We said: 'Whoever among is able (he will)?' So he said: 'When the sun appeared over there (east) like it appears here (west) at Asr, the Messenger of Allah would pray two Rak'ah, and when the sun appeared over there (east) like it appears here (west) at Zuhr, he would pray four Rak'ah. And he would pray four before Zuhr and two after it, and four before Asr separating between every two Rak'ah with At-Taslim upon the angels that are close (to Allah) and those who follow them among the believers, and the Muslims",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-598-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-598-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-598-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b478",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 599,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "(Another chain) from Ali :from the Prophet similarly (no)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-599-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b479",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 600,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah would not pray in women's covers",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-600-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-600-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-600-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-600-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 601,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "Urwah narrated that Aishah said:\"I came while the Messenger of Allah was praying in the house and the door was closed. So he walked until he opened the door for me, then he returned to his place.\" And she described the door to be in the direction of the Qiblah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-601-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-601-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-601-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-601-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 602,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "Abu Wa'il said:\"A man asked Abdullah bin Mas'ud about this phrase: 'Ghairi asin' or is it Yasin? So he said: 'You can recite all of the Quran besides this [phrase]?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Indeed a people recite it, disbursing it like Ad-Daqqa are dispersed, without it passing their throats. Indeed I am aware of the surahs that are comparable which the Messenger of Allah would recite together.'\" He said: \"So we told Alqamah to ask him (what they were). He said: \"Twenty surahs from the Mufassal from which the Prophet would combine, reciting every two Surah in a Rak'ah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-602-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-602-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-602-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-602-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 603,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \"When a man performs Wudu and he performs his Wudu well, then he leaves to the Salat, and he did not leave - or he said: He had no urge - except for it, then there is not one step that he takes except that Allah raises him a degree from it, or removes a sin from him for it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-603-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-603-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-603-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-603-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 604,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "Sa'd bin Ishaq bin Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated from his father from his grandfather who said:\"The Prophet prayed Maghrib in the Masjid of Banu Abdul-Ashbal, and some people stood to offer voluntary prayers, so the Prophet said: 'This Salat is to be performed by you in your homes",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-604-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-604-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-604-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 605,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "Qais bin Asim narrated that:he accepted Islam and the Prophet ordered him to perform Ghusl with water and Sidr",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-605-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-605-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-605-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b47f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 606,
      "bookHadithIndex": 63,
      "text": "Ali bin Abi Talid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \"The screen between the eyes of the jinns and nakedness of the children of Adam when one of you enters the area of relieving oneself is saying: 'Bismillah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-606-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-606-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-606-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b480",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 607,
      "bookHadithIndex": 64,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Busr narrated that :the Prophet said: \"On the day of Resurrection, my nation will be radiant from prostrating and shining from Wudu",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-607-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-607-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-607-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-607-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b481",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 608,
      "bookHadithIndex": 65,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah would love to start with the right side when he purified himself, and when he combed, and when putting his sandals on",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-608-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-608-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-608-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-608-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b482",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 609,
      "bookHadithIndex": 66,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: The acceptable Wudu is with two Ratils of water",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-609-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-609-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-609-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b483",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 610,
      "bookHadithIndex": 67,
      "text": "Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said, about urine of a male child that suckles: \"The urine of the boy is sprinkled, and the girl's urine is washed.\" Qatadah (one of the narrators) said: \"This is so, as long as they do not eat, when they eat, then both of them are washed",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-610-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-610-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-610-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b484",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 611,
      "bookHadithIndex": 68,
      "text": "Shahr bin Hawshab said:\"I saw Jarir bin Abdullah performing Wudu and wiping over his Khuff.\" He said: \"So I asked him: 'What is that?' He said: 'I saw the Prophet performing Wudu and he wiped over his Khuff.' So I said to him: 'Before Al-Ma'idah or after Al-Ma'idah?' He said: 'I did not accept Islam until after Al-Ma'idah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-611-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b485",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 612,
      "bookHadithIndex": 69,
      "text": "Shahr bin Hawshab said:(Another chain) from Khalid bin Ziyad with similar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-612-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b486",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 613,
      "bookHadithIndex": 70,
      "text": "Ammar narrated:\"The Prophet permitted the Junub when he wanted to eat, drink, or sleep, to perform Wudu like the Wudu for Salat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-613-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-613-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-613-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b487",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 614,
      "bookHadithIndex": 71,
      "text": "Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'I seek refuge in Allah for you O Ka'b bin Ujrah from leader that will be after me. Whoever comes to their doors to approve of their lies and supports them in their oppression, then he is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not meet me at the Hawd. And whoever comes to their doors, or he does not come, and he does not approve of their lies and he does not support them in their oppression, then he is from me and I am from him, and he will meet me at the Hawd. Ka'ab bin Ujrah! Salat is clear proof, and Sawm (fasting) is an impregnable shield, and Sadaqah (charity) extinguishes sins just as water extinguishes fire. O Ka'b bin Ujrah! There is no flesh raised that sprouts from the unlawful except that the Fire is more appropriate for it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-614-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-614-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-614-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b488",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 615,
      "bookHadithIndex": 72,
      "text": "Muhammad said:\"Ibn Numair narrated to us from Ubaidullah bin Musa, from Ghalib\" with this (Hadith)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-6-615-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b489",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 6,
      "hadithIndex": 616,
      "bookHadithIndex": 73,
      "text": "Sulaim bin Amir narrated:\"I heard Abu Umamah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah giving a Khutbah during the Farewell Hajj, and he said: 'Have Taqwa of your Lord, and pray your five (prayers), and fast your month, and pay the Zakat on your wealth, and obey thosewho are in charge of you, you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.'\" He said: \"I said to Abu Umamah: 'How old were you when you heard this Hadith (from the Messenger of Allah)?' He said: 'I heard it when I was thirty years old",
